{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1890","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Doremy's Paint 3"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An array $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ of positive integers is good if all the sums of two adjacent elements are equal to the same value. More formally, the array is good if there exists a $$$k$$$ such that $$$b_1 + b_2 = b_2 + b_3 = \\ldots = b_{n-1} + b_n = k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Doremy has an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$. Now Doremy can permute its elements (change their order) however she wants. Determine if she can make the array good."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\le t\\le 100$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 100$$$) — the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$ n $$$ integers $$$ a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n $$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are no constraints on the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes), if it is possible to make the array good, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (upper or lower). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as positive responses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2\n8 9\n3\n1 1 2\n4\n1 1 4 5\n5\n2 3 3 3 3\n4\n100000 100000 100000 100000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYes\nYes\nNo\nNo\nYes\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, $$$[8,9]$$$ and $$$[9,8]$$$ are good."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, $$$[1,2,1]$$$ is good because $$$a_1+a_2=a_2+a_3=3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, it can be shown that no permutation is good."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1890A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1890/problem/A"}